  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "automated-microscopy-2e31",
  "summary": "Recent releases of TISCH3, CROST 2.0 and PDAC BioPortal place spatial tumour transcriptomics inside queryable public resources.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the consolidation of tumour transcriptomic data into queryable public resources, with spatial context increasingly built into the analysis layer. TISCH3 expands to 477 datasets, including 69 spatial transcriptomics collections, while CROST 2.0 extends its spatial repository to 544 projects and 3538 samples with niche, colocalization and cancer-niche tools. PDAC BioPortal integrates bulk, single-nucleus and spatial pancreatic cohorts with pathway and survival analysis. On the method side, SpaceMACE extends MACE to spatial transcriptomics, combining cell-type classification, CNV inference and spatial information for tumour-cell annotation. A pan-cancer single-cell screen across 42 cancers reports conserved tumour microenvironment programs and releases an atlas with scTME software. The items are not uniformly spatial; bulk and single-cell resources, such as the lung RNA-seq study of 1,824 tumours, also feature.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
